k factors)", "Systemic constitutional symptoms (fatigue, malaise)"]}, "branches": {"B1": {"id": "B1", "label": "Counter-Regulatory Hormone Excess / Paraneoplastic Endocrine Syndrome", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "live", "prior": 0.5824698402409769, "posterior": 0.4934932563571598, "danger": 0.8, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.5, "evidence_for": [], "evidence_against": ["The subacute progression and obesity provide weak clinical support for insulin resistance as the primary mechanism, aligning with the typical chronicity of met…"], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": [], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 2.0, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.7, "interrupt_relevance": 0.7, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "mechanism", "representative_diseases": []}, "B2": {"id": "B2", "label": "Insulin Deficiency (Beta-Cell Loss)", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "live", "prior": 0.41640554307394056, "posterior": 0.5063269551760192, "danger": 0.6, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.5, "evidence_for": [], "evidence_against": ["The subacute progression and obesity provide weak clinical support for insulin resistance as the primary mechanism, aligning with the typical chronicity of met…"], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": [], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 2.0, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.5, "interrupt_relevance": 0.5, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "mechanism", "representative_diseases": []}, "B3": {"id": "B3", "label": "Insulin Resistance", "level": 1, "status": "closed_for_now", "posterior": 0.0, "danger": 0.6, "parent": "ROOT", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["While the painful rash is less typical for insulin resistance, the absence of more specific dermatologic features of paraneoplastic syndromes and the subacute …"]}, "B4": {"id": "B4", "label": "Insulin Excess / Hypoglycemia Distractor", "level": 1, "status": "closed_for_now", "posterior": 0.0, "danger": 0.3, "parent": "ROOT", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["A glucose level >500 mg/dL definitively excludes insulin excess as the mechanism. Hypoglycemia would be expected in insulinoma or exogenous insulin administrat…"]}}, "frontier": ["B1", "B2"], "other_mass": 0.0, "pending_results": [], "actions_taken": [{"t": 2, "type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the absence of rapid-onset symptoms and presence of obesity with subacute hyperglycemia and rash argue against beta-cell destruction and support insulin resistance?", "summary": "The lack of rapid-onset symptoms and presence of metabolic risk factors (obesity) reduce the likelihood of B2 and moderately support B3."}, {"t": 2, "type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the presence of a painful rash with systemic symptoms (fatigue, malaise, diarrhea) argue against insulin resistance as the primary mechanism?", "summary": "Painful rashes are less commonly associated with insulin resistance, but this is outweighed by the subacute course and obesity, resulting in a weak reduction for B3."}, {"t": 3, "type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the presence of a painful erythematous rash with papules and plaques, combined with constitutional symptoms and severe hyperglycemia, align with paraneoplastic dermatologic syndromes (e.g., acan…", "summary": "Painful rashes with papules/plaques are not classic features of paraneoplastic dermatologic syndromes like acanthosis nigricans or erythema ab igne, which are typically non-painful and more chronic. This weakens support for B1 and adds neutral/weak evidence for B3."}, {"t": 3, "type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the subacute progression of symptoms over days contradict the typical acute presentation of paraneoplastic endocrine syndromes, thereby favoring insulin resistance (B3) or chronic metabolic proc…", "summary": "The subacute timeline is atypical for paraneoplastic syndromes (B1), which usually present acutely, and this moderately reduces B1’s likelihood. The same timeline aligns better with chronic metabolic processes like insulin resistance (B3), moderately supporting it."}, {"t": 4, "type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the patient’s obesity and subacute progressive hyperglycemia (with constitutional and gastrointestinal symptoms) strongly support insulin resistance as the underlying mechanism?", "summary": "The subacute progression and obesity provide weak clinical support for insulin resistance as the primary mechanism, aligning with the typical chronicity of metabolic disorders."}, {"t": 4, "type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the presence of a painful erythematous rash with papules and plaques argue against insulin resistance as the primary mechanism?", "summary": "While the painful rash is less typical for insulin resistance, the absence of more specific dermatologic features of paraneoplastic syndromes and the subacute course maintain moderate support for B1 and neutral impact on B3."}], "differential_history": [{"top": [["B1", 0.576], ["B2", 0.322], ["B3", 0.075]]}, {"top": [["B1", 0.688], ["B2", 0.301], ["B4", 0.007]]}, {"top": [["B1", 0.582], ["B2", 0.416], ["B4", 0.001]]}], "deliberation": {}, "interrupt": {"active": false, "reason": "No immediate life-threatening instability markers present", "required_actions": []}, "termination": {"ready_to_stop": false, "termination_type": "continue", "reason": "Leading terminal branch (B1) has posterior < 0.75 and dangerous alternative (B1) with posterior >= 0.582 and danger >= 0.8 remains unresolved. Info_exhaustion conditions not met (estimated_remaining_value=0.95)."}, "turn_budget_used": 3, "estimated_remaining_value": 1.1, "max_turn_budget": 5, "latest_action_type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "diagnosis_readiness_score": 0.5824698402409769, "benchmark_output_ready": false, "static_question": "Which of the following is the most likely underlying pathophysiology of this patient’s condition?", "static_options": [{"id": "A", "description": "Alpha cell tumor"}, {"id": "B", "description": "Beta cell destruction"}, {"id": "C", "description": "Beta cell tumor"}, {"id": "D", "description": "Hypercortisolism"}, {"id": "E", "description": "Insulin resistance"}], "seen_evidence_ids": [], "seen_evidence_phenotypes": "{'Abnormality of the endocrine system', 'Insulin resistance', 'Abnormal insulin level', 'Insulin insensitivity', 'Intermittent generalized erythematous papular rash'}", "mode_policy": {"benchmark_purity": true, "allow_external_knowledge": true}, "answer_option_mapping": {}, "tool_use_log": [], "root_revision_needed": false, "program_faults": [], "max_tree_depth": 3, "reasoning_ledger": {"anchor": {"hypothesis": "B1", "t": 0, "posterior_at_anchor": 0.576}, "leader": {"branch_id": "B2", "label": "Insulin Deficiency (Beta-Cell Loss)", "posterior": 0.506, "leading_since_t": 0, "n_revisions": 0}, "leader_evidence": {"confirming": 0, "disconfirming": 5, "last_disconfirming_digest": "The subacute progression and obesity provide weak clinical support for insulin resistance as the primary mechanism, ali…"}, "action_intents": [{"t": 2, "intent": "refute"}, {"t": 2, "intent": "broaden"}, {"t": 3, "intent": "broaden"}, {"t": 3, "intent": "broaden"}, {"t": 4, "intent": "refute"}, {"t": 4, "intent": "broaden"}], "considered_alternatives": ["B1"]}}, "parent_branch": {"id": "B1", "label": "Counter-Regulatory Hormone Excess / Paraneoplastic Endocrine Syndrome", "level": 1, "posterior": 0.4934932563571598, "danger": 0.8, "evidence_for": [], "evidence_against": ["Painful erythematous rash with papules/plaques is less typical of paraneoplastic dermatitis compared to classical necrolytic migratory erythema. The absence of target lesion distribution weakens this association.", "Obesity combined with subacute hyperglycemia is characteristic of progressive insulin resistance. Constitutional symptoms align with metabolic decompensation in type 2 diabetes.", "Paraneoplastic syndromes